  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1404.03 Off-Specification Used Oil",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1404.03 Off-Specification Used Oil.\n\n(a) Used oil shall be classified as off-specification used oil if it:\n\n(1) Exceeds one or more of the standards in Table 14.1, except as provided in (c), below;\n\n(2) Satisfies the rebuttable presumption pursuant to Env-Hw 1402.02(d), as applicable; and\n\n(3) Except as specified in Env-Hw 1402.03(b), has not been mixed with any other hazardous waste.\n\n(b) A used oil handler that blends off-specification used oil to meet the specification used oil standards in Env-Hw 1404.02 shall comply with the requirements for used oil processors/re-refiners in Env-Hw 1408.\n\n(c) Used oil containing PCBs at concentrations of 50 ppm or greater shall not be classified as off-specification used oil and instead shall be regulated as specified in Env-Hw 1402.09(c).\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
